    "text": "Dominica ramis palmarum Passio domini nostri iesu cristi secundum matheum Men \u00f0a leofestan \u00feis is\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0, se h\u00e6lend, to his \u00feegnum, Wita\u00f0 ge \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6fter twegra daga f\u00e6ce Eastron geweor\u00f0a\u00f0, and\n\u00dea w\u00e6ron gegaderode \u00fea witan on \u00f0one cafertun \u00fe\u00e6s ealdormannes, se w\u00e6s gecweden Caiphas, and hi\nHi cw\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t hi noldon on \u00f0am symbeld\u00e6ge \u00fe\u00e6t don, \u00fey l\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t folc onstyred wurde.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s se h\u00e6lend on Bethania on Simones huse \u00fe\u00e6s lic\u00feroweres, \u00fea eode an wif to him and h\u00e6fde an\n\u00dea gesawon \u00fe\u00e6t his \u00feegnas, and hi w\u00e6ron swi\u00f0e yrre, and hi cw\u00e6don, Hw\u00e6t; \u00feeos forswellednys mihte\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend to heom, To hwan yrsige ge wi\u00f0 \u00feis wif?\nSo\u00f0lice god weorc heo w\u00e6s wyrcende on me.\n\u00deearfan ge habba\u00f0 symle mid eow, ac witodlice ne h\u00e6bbe ge me mid eow.\nAnd \u00feeos smyring sceal beon mid minum lichaman, on minre byrigenne.\nAnd so\u00f0lice swa hw\u00e6r swa \u00feis Godspel bi\u00f0 gebodod on eallum middanearde, \u00fe\u00e6r bi\u00f0 ges\u00e6d hire\n\u00dea eode an of \u00f0am twelf apostolum se w\u00e6s gecweden Iudas Scario\u00f0, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00f0am ealdormannum\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don hi \u00fe\u00e6t hi woldon him sellan \u00ferittig seolfer sticca, and he \u00f0a sohte for\u00f0 hu he hine beswican\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don \u00fea \u00feegnas to \u00f0am h\u00e6lende, Hw\u00e6r wilt \u00feu \u00fe\u00e6t we gegearwian \u00fee \u00feas Eastron?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend, Ga\u00f0 in \u00f0as ceastre to \u00f0am men, and secga\u00f0 him \u00fe\u00e6t ic wille wyrcan \u00feas Eastron\n\u00dea dydon \u00fea \u00feegnas swa him se h\u00e6lend bebead, and gegearwodon him \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fea Eastron.\n\u00dea so\u00f0lice w\u00e6s geworden on \u00e6fen \u00fe\u00e6t se h\u00e6lend s\u00e6t \u00e6t his gereordum, and him to cw\u00e6\u00f0, So\u00f0lice ic\n\u00dea wurdon hi ealle swi\u00f0e geunrotsode and heora \u00e6lc cw\u00e6\u00f0, Cwyst \u00feu eom ic hit drihten?\nHe him andswarode and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Se \u00f0e his hand de\u00f0 on minan disce se me sele\u00f0, and witodlice hit geg\u00e6\u00f0\nSo\u00f0lice \u00feeah hw\u00e6re \u00fea \u00feam menn \u00fee \u00feurh hine mannes sunu bi\u00f0 geseald.\nBetere him w\u00e6re \u00fe\u00e6t he n\u00e6fre mann acenned n\u00e6 w\u00e6re.\n\u00dea andswarode him Iudas \u00fee hine sealde, and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Cwyst \u00feu eom ic hit drihten?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu cw\u00e6de.\n\u00dea genam se h\u00e6lend hlaf and hine bletsode and br\u00e6c and sealde his \u00feegnum, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to heom, Onfo\u00f0\nAnd he onfeng calice and hine bletsode and Gode \u00feancas dyde and sealde his \u00feegnum, and cw\u00e6\u00f0,\nSo\u00f0lice ic eow secge, ne drince ic heononfor\u00f0 of \u00f0ysum wincynne \u00e6r on \u00f0am d\u00e6ge \u00fee ic eft drince mid\nAnd \u00fea mid lofsangum gecwedenum, hio eodon on \u00f0\u00e6re dune Oliueti, and \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend to him,\nSwa hit awriten is, swilce man ofslea \u00feone hyrde \u00feonne beo\u00f0 \u00fea sceap to scacene, and \u00e6fter \u00feam \u00fee ic\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Petrus to him, \u00feeah \u00f0e hi \u00f0e ealle swicen n\u00e6fre ic \u00fee ne swice.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend to him, So\u00f0 is \u00fe\u00e6t ic secge \u00fe\u00e6t on \u00f0isse nihte \u00e6r \u00f0an se hana singe\u00f0 \u00feriwe \u00feu me\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Petrus, \u00e6r \u00f0an ic swelte mid \u00fee, \u00e6r ic \u00fee aswice.\nGelice ealle \u00fea \u00feegnas \u00fe\u00e6t ilce cw\u00e6don.\n\u00dea com se h\u00e6lend mid heom on \u00f0one tun se is gecweden Gezamani.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he to his \u00feegnum, Sitta\u00f0 her o\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t ic gange \u00feider and ic me \u00fe\u00e6r gebidde.\nAnd hi w\u00e6ron swi\u00f0e geunrotsode.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend to heom, Unrot is min sawul o\u00f0 dea\u00f0.\nOnbida\u00f0 her and wacia\u00f0 mid me.\nAnd he eode and hine geb\u00e6d and com eft to his \u00feegnum, and gemette hi sl\u00e6pende and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Petre,\nWacia\u00f0, and gebidda\u00f0 eow \u00fe\u00e6t ge ne gangan on costunga.\nWitodlice in gast fus, and min fl\u00e6sc untrum.\nAnd eft he eode and hine geb\u00e6d, and com eft, and gemette hi sl\u00e6pende, and heora eagan w\u00e6ron swi\u00f0e\nNu to geneal\u00e6ce\u00f0 seo tid \u00fe\u00e6t mannes sunu bi\u00f0 geseald on synfulra handa.\nArisa\u00f0 and uton gangan nu to geneal\u00e6ca\u00f0 se \u00f0e me selle\u00f0.\n\u00dea com Iudas se \u00f0e hine sealde, and mid him com micel m\u00e6nigo mid sweordum and mid stengum fram\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Iudas Scario\u00f0 l\u00e6wend, Swa hwylcne swa ic cysse nima\u00f0 \u00feone.\nAnd sona he eode to \u00f0am h\u00e6lende, and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Wes \u00feu hal lareow?\nAnd hine cyste.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend to him, \u00feu freond, to hwan come \u00feu?\nHi \u00f0a eodon to \u00f0am h\u00e6lende, and hine bundon.\n\u00dea Petrus ut abr\u00e6d his sweord and sloh Malchus \u00feone \u00feeow, and his eare of asloh.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend to him, Gecyr \u00fein swurd on his sc\u00e6\u00f0e.\nSo\u00f0lice ealle \u00fea \u00f0e onfo\u00f0 sweord mid sweorde hi forwur\u00f0a\u00f0.\nAc hwi ne wenst \u00feu \u00fe\u00e6t ic ne mihte biddan minne f\u00e6der \u00fe\u00e6t he me gegearwode ma \u00feonne twelf\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend to \u00f0am m\u00e6nigum, Nu ge comon mid sweordum and mid stencgum and me\nAc so\u00f0lice \u00feis is eall geworden \u00fe\u00e6tte w\u00e6ron gefyllede \u00fea gewritu \u00fe\u00e6ra witegena.\n\u00dea \u00feegnas \u00fea ealle forleton \u00feone h\u00e6lend and him fram flugon, and hi \u00f0a l\u00e6ddon \u00feone h\u00e6lend\nAnd Petrus w\u00e6s feorran fyligende o\u00f0 \u00f0one cafertun, and \u00fe\u00e6r \u00e6t \u00f0am gate ges\u00e6t mid \u00f0am \u00feegnum \u00fe\u00e6t\nAnd hi \u00f0a sohton ealle lease gecy\u00f0nyssa ongean \u00feone h\u00e6lend \u00fe\u00e6t hio hine to dea\u00f0e gesealdon, and\n\u00dees cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ic m\u00e6g towurpan Godes tempel, and \u00e6fter \u00fereora daga f\u00e6ce eft hit getimbrian.\n\u00dea aras se ealdor \u00fe\u00e6ra sacerda and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him, Ic \u00f0e halsige \u00feurh God \u00fe\u00e6ne lifigendan \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu secge\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se h\u00e6lend to him, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu cw\u00e6de.\nSo\u00f0lice ic secge eow heononfor\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t ge geseo\u00f0 mannes sunu sittende on \u00f0a swi\u00f0ran healfe Godes\n\u00dea sona se ealdorman slat his hr\u00e6gl, and \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0, He yfel sacode.\nHw\u00e6t be\u00f0urfon we nu ofer \u00feis leasra cy\u00f0era?\nNu we gehyrdon his yfelsacunga.\nAc hw\u00e6t is eow ge\u00f0uht be \u00f0am?\n\u00dea andswaredon hi ealle and cw\u00e6don, Dea\u00f0es he is scyldig.\n\u00dea sp\u00e6tton hi on his ansyne and mid fystum hine swungon, sume bradum handum on his neb slogon,\nAnd Petrus s\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6rute on \u00f0am cafertune, and \u00fea eode to him an mennen, and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Come \u00feu mid\nAnd he wi\u00f0soc beforan him eallum, and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Nat ic hw\u00e6t \u00feu m\u00e6nst.\n\u00dea eode \u00fe\u00e6r o\u00f0er m\u00e6nnen to \u00f0\u00e6re duru and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00f0am \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6rute w\u00e6ron, \u00fees w\u00e6s mid \u00feam\nAnd eft he wi\u00f0soc mid a\u00f0swara, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he ne cu\u00f0e \u00feone mann.\nAnd \u00e6fter lytlum f\u00e6ce \u00fea \u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6r stodon hi cw\u00e6don to Petre, So\u00f0lice \u00feu come mid \u00feam h\u00e6lende.\n\u00dein spr\u00e6c \u00fee swutela\u00f0.\nAnd he \u00f0a gyt \u00e6tsoc mid a\u00f0sweringe, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he ne cu\u00f0e \u00feone man, and \u00fea sona se hana creow.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s Petrus swi\u00f0e gemyndig \u00fe\u00e6s wordes \u00fee se h\u00e6lend cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00e6r \u00f0an se hana singe \u00feriwa \u00feu me\nAnd he \u00fea ut eode, and ongan wepan swi\u00f0e biterlice.\nAnd \u00fea on \u00e6rnemerigen hi worhton ge\u00feeaht ongean \u00feone h\u00e6lend \u00fe\u00e6t hi hine to dea\u00f0e gesealdon.\nAnd hi hine \u00fea l\u00e6ddon gebundenne to \u00f0am Pontiscan Pilate, \u00feam gerefan.\n\u00dea geseah Iudas se \u00f0e hine sealde \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6s fordemed, \u00fea wolde he don d\u00e6dbote and gebrohte \u00fea\nAnd hi cw\u00e6don, Hw\u00e6t wilt \u00feu us \u00fe\u00e6t witen?\nAnd hi \u00f0a awurpon \u00feam seolfor sticcan in to \u00f0am temple.\nAnd he \u00f0a ut eode and hine sylfne on grine aheng.\nAnd \u00fea ealdormen \u00fea cw\u00e6don, Nis na \u00feis feoh alyfed to donne on ure madmcyste, for \u00f0an hit is\n\u00dea worhton hi ge\u00f0eaht and gebohton \u00fe\u00e6r mid an land heore tigelwyrhtum, \u00fe\u00e6t land is gecweden\n\u00dea w\u00e6s gefylled \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6r w\u00e6s gecweden \u00feurh Hieremiam \u00feone witegan \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde beon geboht\n\u00dea stod se h\u00e6lend beforan \u00feam gerefan, and he cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him, Eart \u00feu cyning Iudea?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him se h\u00e6lend, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu cwyst.\nAnd he w\u00e6s gewreged fram \u00feam ealdormannum and \u00feam witum.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him Pilatus, Ne gehyrst \u00feu hu feala ongean \u00fee secga\u00f0 \u00feas gecy\u00f0nesse?\nAnd \u00feu him ne andswarast mid \u00e6nige worde.\n\u00dea sceolde se gerefa on \u00f0am symbeld\u00e6ge forl\u00e6tan \u00feam folce \u00e6nne gebundenne r\u00e6pling swylcne hi\n\u00dea w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6r an m\u00e6re r\u00e6pling, se w\u00e6s gecweden Barrabban.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Pilatus to \u00f0am folc, Hw\u00e6\u00f0erne wille ge \u00fe\u00e6t ic eow forl\u00e6te \u00fee \u0